      "question": {
        ":question/id": "114d0a46-d76c-5c09-b066-e75e6125cdb9",
        ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 58 & -16 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{23}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+4R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}22 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}+9R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}22 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 58 & -16 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+4R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}+9R_{2}$.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
